# vehje-runtime-abi. wire family

The framework's per-script wire family and C ABI. The residual as a
control-flow-graph-of-blocks arena (block and function tables), the value-arena
a produced value crosses back in (children-first, no back-patch, region-table
indirection), the reserve-commit two-function sink contract, the diagnostics
schema, and the one runtime-W batched-column `extern "C"` entry (W at least two,
an `Outcome`-in-the-value-arena return). One crate split into `wire`, `value`,
`sink`, and `entry` modules, because the residual arena and value-arena are one
structural family with one record-layout definition. Pure `#[repr(C)]` type
surface, no runtime logic. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
